A colleague proposes this fix in OpenRamble's `DictationController`.

Their description: "A press that arrives while a paste is finishing is queued and replayed after it. A hands-free take ends with a second press, and that second press was ignored during the paste, so the replayed take listened forever. Now the second press is recorded and replayed too."

For context, this is `stop()` as it is today. It is called when the dictation key is released:

```swift
    /// The hotkey is released (or pressed a second time in hands-free mode).
    public func stop() {
        if state == .inserting, pressDuringInsertion != nil {
            // The release of a press that waits for the paste: it is replayed
            // with it, so a tap stays a tap and no key that is up keeps the
            // microphone on.
            pressDuringInsertion?.released = true
            return
        }
        switch DictationStopPolicy.decideStop(state: state, isHandsFree: isHandsFree) {
        case .stopNow:
            markStopRequested()
            finish()
        case .deferUntilListening:
            markStopRequested()
            deferredStopRequested = true
            if let session = currentSession { stopArrivedBeforeTheMicrophoneOpened(session: session) }
        case .ignore, .noSession:
            break
        }
    }

    /// Stop in the mode without holding - by pressing the key a second time.
```

The rule in this app is that a hands-free take ends only with a second press, and releasing the key means nothing in hands-free mode.

The proposed change:

```diff
diff --git a/Packages/DictationCore/Sources/DictationCore/DictationController.swift b/Packages/DictationCore/Sources/DictationCore/DictationController.swift
index 87695d9..61cfcfe 100644
--- a/Packages/DictationCore/Sources/DictationCore/DictationController.swift
+++ b/Packages/DictationCore/Sources/DictationCore/DictationController.swift
@@ -699,6 +699,11 @@ public final class DictationController {

     /// Stop in the mode without holding - by pressing the key a second time.
     public func stopHandsFree() {
+        if state == .inserting, pressDuringInsertion != nil {
+            // The second press of a press that waits for the paste.
+            pressDuringInsertion?.released = true
+            return
+        }
         guard isHandsFree else { return }

         switch state {
@@ -1742,7 +1747,9 @@ public final class DictationController {
         await end(session, saying: notice)
         if let press {
             begin(handsFree: press.handsFree, isEnabled: press.isEnabled, isModelReady: press.isModelReady)
-            if press.released { stop() }
+            if press.released {
+                if press.handsFree { stopHandsFree() } else { stop() }
+            }
         }
     }
```

Review this change.
